#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Decide the next step of the orca-kit:spec-review revision loop.

Usage:
  converge [--repo ROOT] [--record FILE] [--previous PREV.md] <spec.md>
  converge --rules

  --repo ROOT     As for gate: where .orca-kit/spec-review.yml is read from.
                  Defaults to the nearest directory at or above the spec with
                  .orca-kit/ or .git.
  --record FILE   The review record. Defaults to specs/reviews/<slug>.json
                  next to the spec.
  --previous P    The spec as it was before the author's last revision.
                  Not allowed on pass 1. From pass 2 on it defaults to the
                  snapshot of the pass before, kept beside the record
                  (v0.8): specs/reviews/<slug>/pass-<n-1>/<slug>.md. Given,
                  it overrides the snapshot; with neither, exit 2.
  --rules         List the stop reasons, and exit.

The loop (docs/spec-review/ROADMAP.md, v0.5, and loop.md next to this
script): the record's `passes` hold one entry per review pass, the last one
being the review of <spec.md> as it is now. This script reads the record,
re-runs the hard gates on the spec, counts its words, and prints one verdict:

  converged   the last pass has no open blockers and the gates pass
  continue    the last pass has only `fix` blockers, fewer than before, and
              there is a pass left: hand those blockers to the author
  stop        anything else, with one reason, checked in this order:
    bloat-ceiling  the revision put the spec over max_words
    bloat-growth   the revision grew the spec by more than max_growth
    gate           a hard gate fails on the spec
    oscillation    the pass has a new blocker in a section the revision changed
    no-progress    open blockers didn't strictly decrease
    decision       an open blocker is `kind: decision`, for the user
    cap            pass 3 still has open blockers

Two blockers are the same blocker across passes when they have the same
`rule` and the same `location.section` (ignoring case and runs of
whitespace), counted as a multiset; line, ref and wording are ignored,
because a revision moves lines and fresh reviewers word and anchor the same
problem differently. A blocker is new when the pass before had no blocker
with its rule and section. A new blocker is oscillation only when the
revision caused it: its section's text differs between --previous and the
spec (sections are the `## ` headings outside code, compared by heading,
ignoring case and runs of whitespace, and by their lines with trailing
spaces dropped; a section missing from either file counts as changed). A new
blocker in a section the revision didn't touch was caught late: it is
reported as a `note [loop.late]` line, and the loop goes on if open blockers
still strictly fell (otherwise it stops with no-progress). The bloat checks
and the section comparison need --previous, so they run from pass 2 on;
growth is (words - previous words) / previous words.

Answered decisions (v0.6, pauses.md): the record's `questions` hold the
user's answers. A decision blocker whose question was answered with a choice
that resolves it (a lettered option, `other`, or `keep` for the slicer) no longer
stops the loop: it is handed to the author with the fix blockers, and a pass
follows to apply it. It still counts as open in the pass it was raised in,
so the next pass must have strictly fewer. The slicer's slicer.oversized
blocker, once the user answered `keep`, is not open again in later passes:
the user already chose. Any other decision raised again is open again, and
asked again, since it may be a new question. Answers add no passes; pass 3 is still the last. With no
`questions`, the verdict is exactly v0.5's.

Prints, in the gate's format, one line per problem behind a stop:
  <file>:<line>: error [loop.<reason>] <section>: <problem>. Fix: <what to do>.
one note per blocker caught late, and one per answered decision:
  <file>:<line>: note [loop.late] <section>: <problem>. Fix: <what to do>.
  <file>:<line>: note [loop.answered] <section>: <problem>. Fix: <what to do>.
then a status line and the verdict:
  <file>: pass 2 of 3: 1 open blocker (1 fix, 0 decision), was 3, 1 new (0 in changed sections); 640 words, was 612 (+4.6%); gates ok
  <file>: continue to pass 3: hand 1 fix blocker to the author
  <file>: continue to pass 2: hand 1 fix blocker and 1 answer to the author
  <file>: converged at pass 2
  <file>: stop at pass 2: oscillation

Settings, in .orca-kit/spec-review.yml next to the gate's (gate --help):
  max_words: 2000     # the length ceiling, also the bloat ceiling
  max_growth: 0.25    # the most a revision may grow the spec in one pass

Snapshots (v0.8): the skill keeps each pass's reviewed spec beside the
record, at specs/reviews/<slug>/pass-<n>/<slug>.md (under the spec's own
name, so gate gives it the spec's result; `check specs/*.md` doesn't reach
it). From them every pass's verdict can be recomputed from what is in the
repo: pass n's previous spec is pass n-1's snapshot. When pass n's own
snapshot exists, the spec given must match it (exit 2 if not), so a verdict
is never computed for another text. To recheck the last pass after the spec
has moved on, give its snapshot as the spec and the record with --record.

Every input is a file, so the same record and specs always get the same
verdict. This script only reads files; it never edits the spec or the record.

Exit codes: 0 converged, 1 stop, 3 continue, 2 a usage error, an unreadable
or unparseable spec, an invalid settings file or record, a record with no
passes, pass 2 or 3 with neither --previous nor a snapshot of the pass
before, a spec that differs from its pass's snapshot, or a record whose
`words` or `gates` don't match the specs given.

Python 3 standard library only; no install step.
"""

import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import sys
from collections import Counter

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))


def load_sibling(name):
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("spec_review_" + name, os.path.join(HERE, name))
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader))
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


GATE = load_sibling("gate")
RECORD = GATE.RECORD
FINDINGS = GATE.FINDINGS

MAX_PASSES = RECORD.MAX_PASSES
REASONS = ("bloat-ceiling", "bloat-growth", "gate", "oscillation", "no-progress", "decision", "cap")

RULE_TEXT = {
    "loop.bloat-ceiling": "stop: the revision put the spec over the length ceiling (max_words)",
    "loop.bloat-growth": "stop: the revision grew the spec by more than max_growth of its previous words in one pass",
    "loop.gate": "stop: a hard gate fails on the spec (run gate for its lines)",
    "loop.oscillation": "stop: the pass has a blocker (rule and section) the pass before didn't, in a section the revision changed",
    "loop.late": "note: a new blocker in a section the revision didn't change was caught late; not oscillation",
    "loop.answered": "note: a decision blocker the user answered (record questions, v0.6) goes to the author; a slicer.oversized blocker kept in an earlier pass isn't open again",
    "loop.no-progress": "stop: the open-blocker count didn't strictly decrease",
    "loop.decision": "stop: an open blocker is kind decision, a question for the user",
    "loop.cap": "stop: pass %d still has open blockers" % MAX_PASSES,
}

USAGE = ("usage: converge [--repo ROOT] [--record FILE] [--previous PREV.md] <spec.md>\n"
         "       converge --rules")


class UsageError(Exception):
    pass


class InputError(Exception):
    """A problem with the inputs that stops the verdict (exit 2); the lines to print."""

    def __init__(self, lines):
        Exception.__init__(self, lines[0] if lines else "")
        self.lines = lines


# The counting rule lives in record (v0.8), so the record's stored open_blockers,
# this verdict, pause and summary can't count differently.
plural = RECORD.plural
blocker_key = RECORD.blocker_key
blockers_of = RECORD.blockers_of
resolutions = RECORD.resolutions
open_of = RECORD.open_of


def new_blockers(current, previous):
    """The blockers of `current` beyond what `previous` had, per key, in order."""
    room = Counter(blocker_key(f) for f in previous)
    out = []
    for f in current:
        key = blocker_key(f)
        if room[key] > 0:
            room[key] -= 1
        else:
            out.append(f)
    return out


def snapshot_path(record_path, slug, pass_no):
    """Where a pass's reviewed spec is kept beside the record (v0.8): specs/reviews/<slug>/pass-<n>/<slug>.md."""
    return os.path.join(os.path.dirname(record_path), slug, "pass-%d" % pass_no, slug + ".md")


def sections_of(text):
    """{heading: text} for each `## ` section of a spec, outside code; headings ignore case and spacing."""
    doc = GATE.Doc(text)
    out, current = {}, None
    for i in range(doc.body_start, len(doc.lines)):
        line = doc.lines[i]
        if not doc.in_code[i] and line.startswith("## "):
            current = FINDINGS._norm(line[3:])
            out[current] = []
        elif current is not None:
            out[current].append(line.rstrip())
    return dict((k, "\n".join(v).strip("\n")) for k, v in out.items())


def changed_sections(text, previous_text):
    """The headings (normalised) whose text differs between the two specs, or that only one of them has."""
    a, b = sections_of(text), sections_of(previous_text)
    return set(k for k in set(a) | set(b) if a.get(k) != b.get(k))


def read_spec(path, what):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return f.read()
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e:
        raise InputError(["%s:1: error [usage] file: can't read the %s (%s). Fix: Pass the path to a spec .md file." % (path, what, e)])


def growth_text(words, prev_words):
    if prev_words is None:
        return ""
    if prev_words == 0:
        return ", was 0"
    return ", was %d (%+.1f%%)" % (prev_words, 100.0 * (words - prev_words) / prev_words)


def decide(spec, repo_opt=None, record_path=None, previous=None):
    """(exit code, output lines) for one spec. Raises InputError for exit 2."""
    code, lines, _ = assess(spec, repo_opt, record_path, previous)
    return code, lines


def assess(spec, repo_opt=None, record_path=None, previous=None):
    """(exit code, output lines, state) for one spec; state is what `pause` builds on. Raises InputError for exit 2."""
    text = read_spec(spec, "spec")
    repo = os.path.abspath(repo_opt) if repo_opt else GATE.find_repo(spec)
    try:
        config, _ = GATE.load_config(repo)
    except GATE.ConfigError as e:
        cfg = os.path.relpath(os.path.join(repo, GATE.CONFIG_PATH))
        raise InputError(["%s:%d: error [config] settings: %s. Fix: Correct the settings file; `gate --help` shows the format." % (cfg, e.line, e.message)])

    rec = record_path or GATE.record_path(spec)
    if not os.path.isfile(rec):
        raise InputError(["%s:1: error [loop.record] file: no review record at %s. Fix: Run a review pass and write the record first." % (spec, rec)])
    _, rec_lines, data = RECORD.check_file(rec)
    if data is None:
        raise InputError(rec_lines + ["%s:1: error [loop.record] file: the review record %s isn't valid. Fix: Correct it; `record --help` shows the format." % (spec, rec)])
    passes = data.get("passes")
    if not passes:
        raise InputError(["%s:1: error [loop.record] file: %s has no passes. Fix: Record the review pass before asking for a verdict." % (spec, rec)])
    n = len(passes)
    if n == 1 and previous is not None:
        raise InputError(["%s:1: error [usage] file: pass 1 has no revision, so --previous doesn't apply. Fix: Leave it out." % spec])
    if n >= 2 and previous is None:
        snap = snapshot_path(rec, data["spec"], n - 1)
        if not os.path.isfile(snap):
            raise InputError(["%s:1: error [usage] file: pass %d needs --previous, the spec as it was before the revision, "
                              "and there is no snapshot of pass %d at %s. Fix: Pass the copy saved before the blockers were handed back, "
                              "or keep each pass's reviewed spec at that path." % (spec, n, n - 1, snap)])
        previous = snap
    own = snapshot_path(rec, data["spec"], n)
    if os.path.isfile(own) and read_spec(own, "snapshot of pass %d" % n) != text:
        raise InputError(["%s:1: error [loop.record] file: the spec differs from %s, the snapshot of the pass %d review. "
                          "Fix: Give the spec that pass reviewed, or correct the snapshot." % (spec, own, n)])

    gate_code, gate_lines = GATE.gate_file(spec, repo_opt)
    if gate_code == 2:
        raise InputError(gate_lines)
    gates_ok = gate_code == 0
    words = GATE.count_words(GATE.Doc(text))
    prev_words, changed = None, set()
    if previous is not None:
        prev_text = read_spec(previous, "previous spec")
        prev_words = GATE.count_words(GATE.Doc(prev_text))
        changed = changed_sections(text, prev_text)

    last, before = passes[-1], (passes[-2] if n >= 2 else None)
    mismatch = []
    if "words" in last and last["words"] != words:
        mismatch.append("pass %d records %d words, but %s has %d" % (n, last["words"], spec, words))
    if "gates" in last and last["gates"] != ("passed" if gates_ok else "failed"):
        mismatch.append("pass %d records gates %s, but they %s on %s" % (n, last["gates"], "pass" if gates_ok else "fail", spec))
    if before is not None and "words" in before and before["words"] != prev_words:
        mismatch.append("pass %d records %d words, but %s has %d" % (n - 1, before["words"], previous, prev_words))
    if mismatch:
        raise InputError(["%s:1: error [loop.record] file: %s. Fix: Give the spec this pass reviewed and the copy saved before its revision, "
                          "or correct the record." % (spec, m) for m in mismatch])

    answered, carried = resolutions(data)
    current = open_of(last, n, carried)
    open_n = len(current)
    decisions = [f for f in current if f["kind"] == "decision"]
    answered_now = [f for f in decisions if (n, f["id"]) in answered]
    unanswered = [f for f in decisions if (n, f["id"]) not in answered]
    fixes = open_n - len(decisions)
    before_open = open_of(before, n - 1, carried) if before is not None else None
    new = new_blockers(current, before_open) if before is not None else []
    caused = [f for f in new if FINDINGS._norm(f["location"]["section"]) in changed or
              FINDINGS._norm(f["location"]["section"]) not in sections_of(text)]
    late = [f for f in new if f not in caused]
    was = len(before_open) if before is not None else None

    status = "%s: pass %d of %d: %s (%d fix, %d decision)" % (spec, n, MAX_PASSES, plural(open_n, "open blocker"), fixes, len(decisions))
    if was is not None:
        status += ", was %d, %d new (%d in changed sections)" % (was, len(new), len(caused))
    status += "; %s%s; gates %s" % (plural(words, "word"), growth_text(words, prev_words), "ok" if gates_ok else "failed")

    problems = []
    reason = None
    ceiling, max_growth = config["max_words"], config["max_growth"]

    def problem(line, rule, section, message, fix):
        problems.append("%s:%d: error [loop.%s] %s: %s. Fix: %s." % (spec, line, rule, section, message, fix[0].upper() + fix[1:]))

    if prev_words is not None and words > ceiling:
        reason = "bloat-ceiling"
        problem(1, reason, "file", "the revision made the spec %d words, over the ceiling of %d (it was %d)" % (words, ceiling, prev_words),
                "reject the revision and restore %s; fix blockers by tightening text, not adding paragraphs" % previous)
    elif prev_words is not None and words - prev_words > max_growth * prev_words:
        reason = "bloat-growth"
        problem(1, reason, "file", "the revision grew the spec from %d to %d words, more than max_growth %s of %d in one pass" % (
            prev_words, words, ("%g" % max_growth), prev_words),
            "reject the revision and restore %s; fix blockers by tightening text, not adding paragraphs" % previous)
    elif not gates_ok:
        reason = "gate"
        failed = [l for l in gate_lines if ": gates failed: " in l]
        problem(1, reason, "file", "a hard gate fails (%s)" % (failed[0].split(": gates failed: ", 1)[1] if failed else "see gate"),
                "run gate on the spec for every failing line; the loop goes on only on a spec that passes its gates")
    elif caused:
        reason = "oscillation"
        for f in caused:
            problem(f["location"]["line"] or 1, reason, f["location"]["section"],
                    "blocker %s (%s, %s) is new in pass %d, in a section the revision changed" % (f["rule"], f["id"], f["kind"], n),
                    "stop and ask the user; the revision introduced a blocker, so another pass won't converge")
    elif was is not None and open_n >= was:
        reason = "no-progress"
        problem(1, reason, "file", "pass %d has %d open blockers, not fewer than pass %d's %d" % (n, open_n, n - 1, was),
                "stop and ask the user; more passes won't fix missing context")
    elif open_n == 0:
        reason = None
    elif unanswered:
        reason = "decision"
        for f in unanswered:
            problem(f["location"]["line"] or 1, reason, f["location"]["section"],
                    "blocker %s (%s) is a decision for the user" % (f["rule"], f["id"]),
                    "ask the user, with the options; the author never answers a decision")
    elif n >= MAX_PASSES:
        reason = "cap"
        problem(1, reason, "file", "pass %d of %d still has %s" % (n, MAX_PASSES, plural(open_n, "open blocker")),
                "stop and ask the user; the loop has no passes left")

    notes = ["%s:%d: note [loop.late] %s: blocker %s (%s, %s) is new in pass %d, in a section the revision didn't change. "
             "Fix: Treat it as caught late, not caused by the revision; it is handed back like any other blocker." % (
                 spec, f["location"]["line"] or 1, f["location"]["section"], f["rule"], f["id"], f["kind"], n) for f in late]
    for f in answered_now:
        q = answered[(n, f["id"])]
        notes.append("%s:%d: note [loop.answered] %s: decision blocker %s (%s) is answered (%s: %s). "
                     "Fix: Hand the answer to the author with the fix blockers; the reviewers never see it." % (
                         spec, f["location"]["line"] or 1, f["location"]["section"], f["rule"], f["id"], q["id"], q["answer"]["choice"]))
    for f in blockers_of(last):
        q = carried.get((n, f["id"]))
        if q:
            notes.append("%s:%d: note [loop.answered] %s: decision blocker %s (%s) was answered in pass %d (%s: %s), so it isn't open again. "
                         "Fix: Check the revision applied that answer; don't ask it again." % (
                             spec, f["location"]["line"] or 1, f["location"]["section"], f["rule"], f["id"], q["pass"], q["id"],
                             q["answer"]["choice"]))
    lines = problems + notes + [status]
    state = {"spec": spec, "pass": n, "reason": reason, "open": current, "unanswered": unanswered, "answered_now": answered_now,
             "fixes": fixes, "data": data, "config": config, "text": text, "words": words, "prev_words": prev_words,
             "gates_ok": gates_ok, "gate_lines": gate_lines, "carried": carried, "answered": answered, "record": rec,
             "previous": previous}
    if reason:
        state["verdict"] = "stop"
        return 1, lines + ["%s: stop at pass %d: %s" % (spec, n, reason)], state
    if open_n == 0:
        state["verdict"] = "converged"
        return 0, lines + ["%s: converged at pass %d" % (spec, n)], state
    state["verdict"] = "continue"
    hand = plural(fixes, "fix blocker") + (" and " + plural(len(answered_now), "answer") if answered_now else "")
    return 3, lines + ["%s: continue to pass %d: hand %s to the author" % (spec, n + 1, hand)], state


def parse_args(argv):
    opts = {"mode": "decide", "repo": None, "record": None, "previous": None, "paths": []}
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        arg = argv[i]
        if arg in ("-h", "--help"):
            opts["mode"] = "help"
            return opts
        if arg == "--rules":
            opts["mode"] = "rules"
            return opts
        name = next((k for k in ("repo", "record", "previous") if arg == "--" + k or arg.startswith("--%s=" % k)), None)
        if name:
            if arg == "--" + name:
                if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                    raise UsageError("--%s needs a value" % name)
                value, i = argv[i + 1], i + 2
            else:
                value, i = arg.split("=", 1)[1], i + 1
            if opts[name] is not None:
                raise UsageError("--%s given twice" % name)
            opts[name] = value
            continue
        if arg == "--":
            opts["paths"].extend(argv[i + 1:])
            break
        if arg.startswith("-") and arg != "-":
            raise UsageError("unknown option %r" % arg)
        opts["paths"].append(arg)
        i += 1
    if opts["repo"] is not None and not os.path.isdir(opts["repo"]):
        raise UsageError("--repo %r is not a directory" % opts["repo"])
    if len(opts["paths"]) != 1:
        raise UsageError("give exactly one spec")
    return opts


def main(argv=None):
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    try:
        opts = parse_args(argv)
    except UsageError as e:
        sys.stderr.write("converge: %s\n%s\n" % (e, USAGE))
        return 2
    if opts["mode"] == "help":
        sys.stdout.write(__doc__.lstrip())
        return 0
    if opts["mode"] == "rules":
        for rule_id, text in RULE_TEXT.items():
            print("  %-20s %s" % (rule_id, text))
        return 0
    try:
        code, lines = decide(opts["paths"][0], opts["repo"], opts["record"], opts["previous"])
    except InputError as e:
        code, lines = 2, e.lines
    for line in lines:
        print(line)
    return code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
